00:32:33.320 --> 00:32:47.040
<v Elna Baker>Or two people showed up dressed above and beyond to a costume party, only to find out that it was the wrong day, which also actually happened to me.
<v Elna Baker>那是什么感觉？所以，我猜有几种不同的分类？

00:32:47.040 --> 00:32:51.810
<v Ira Glass>So what was that like? OK, so there are these, I guess, different categories of responses?
<v Ira Glass>基本是这样，同样的事情一遍又一遍出现。

00:32:51.810 --> 00:32:54.920
<v Elna Baker>Yeah, basically, like, the same things came up over and over again.
<v Elna Baker>OK，分类一下主要的。我想听听，第一名是什么？

00:32:54.920 --> 00:32:58.010
<v Ira Glass>OK, break down the big ones. I want to hear, what's the number one?
<v Ira Glass>所以我想说最大的一个，第一名，是浴室故事。大概四分之一的人写了浴室的故事。接着是裸体故事。

00:32:58.010 --> 00:33:08.330
<v Elna Baker>So I would say the biggest one, the number one, was bathroom stories. Like, a quarter-- a quarter of the people who wrote us, bathroom stories. Followed by naked stories.
<v Elna Baker>那是第二名。

00:33:08.330 --> 00:33:09.530
<v Ira Glass>That's number two.
